
An imbalanced bank marketing dataset comprising over 40,000 samples was used to train and evaluate machine learning models for predicting client subscription to a term deposit. Four models were tested: Decision Tree, Random Forest, AdaBoost, and XGBoost. Due to the dataset’s imbalance (approximately 88% “No” and 12% “Yes” responses), the models were expected to be biased toward predicting the majority class. To address this, class weighting and resampling techniques were applied to improve sensitivity toward the minority (positive) class.